25:Tac7,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use Geo Location","description":"Every place on Earth can be described by two numbers: latitude and longitude. This geo location tool finds your current position (only if you allow it), or converts a latitude and longitude pair into a readable address. It is useful for sharing your exact spot, filling GPS fields in forms, checking ","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/geo-location","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"Geo Location"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to use the geo location finder","text":"Press the “use my location” button and allow the browser to share your position to see your latitude, longitude and an approximate address. To look up a point, type the latitude and longitude into the two boxes and press “Reverse geocode address”; the tool then shows the address it belongs to."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Latitude and longitude in plain words","text":"Latitude measures how far north or south of the equator a place is, from 0° to 90°. Longitude measures how far east or west of the prime meridian it is, from 0° to 180°. India lies roughly between 8° and 37° north and 68° and 97° east, so Indian coordinates are usually positive numbers such as 28.6139° N, 77.2090° E for Delhi."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Accuracy and privacy","text":"Position accuracy depends on your device. A phone with GPS outdoors can be accurate to a few metres, while a laptop that uses Wi-Fi location may be off by hundreds of metres. Dense buildings and indoor spaces can reduce accuracy."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Practical uses","text":"Use the coordinates to guide a courier to a hard-to-find address, fill in the location field in a farming, survey or insurance form, or save the position of a parked vehicle. Paste the coordinates into a maps app to open the exact spot."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"What reverse geocoding means","text":"Turning an address into coordinates is called geocoding, and turning coordinates back into an address is reverse geocoding. This tool does the second one. It takes a latitude and longitude, looks up the nearest known road, locality and city in an open map database and returns a readable address."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"Ways to write coordinates","text":"Coordinates appear in three common styles. Decimal degrees, such as 28.6139, 77.2090, are used by this tool and by most apps. Degrees and decimal minutes, such as 28° 36.834′ N, 77° 12.540′ E, appear on some GPS devices. Degrees, minutes and seconds, such as 28° 36′ 50″ N, 77° 12′ 32″ E, appear in older surveys and maps."}]}23:["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$25"}}]
