2f:["$","div","What reverse geocoding means",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"What reverse geocoding means"}],[["$","p","Turning an address into coordinates is called ge",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Turning an address into coordinates is called geocoding, and turning coordinates back into an address is reverse geocoding. This tool does the second one. It takes a latitude and longitude, looks up the nearest known road, locality and city in an open map database and returns a readable address."}],["$","p","Because the address is the nearest match in map ",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Because the address is the nearest match in map data and not a postal record, it may show the neighbouring road, a nearby landmark or only the locality for remote areas. In farmland, forests and new colonies the result can be general, such as a village and district. For an exact delivery address always give the house number and landmark in words as well."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Reverse geocoding returns the nearest mapped address, not a legal address",{"children":"Reverse geocoding returns the nearest mapped address, not a legal address"}],["$","li","Remote locations may show only a village, district or state",{"children":"Remote locations may show only a village, district or state"}],["$","li","Use the PIN code finder to confirm the postal code for the area",{"children":"Use the PIN code finder to confirm the postal code for the area"}]]}],null]}]
30:["$","div","Ways to write coordinates",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"Ways to write coordinates"}],[["$","p","Coordinates appear in three common styles. Decim",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Coordinates appear in three common styles. Decimal degrees, such as 28.6139, 77.2090, are used by this tool and by most apps. Degrees and decimal minutes, such as 28° 36.834′ N, 77° 12.540′ E, appear on some GPS devices. Degrees, minutes and seconds, such as 28° 36′ 50″ N, 77° 12′ 32″ E, appear in older surveys and maps."}],["$","p","To convert degrees, minutes and seconds to decim",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"To convert degrees, minutes and seconds to decimal degrees, divide the minutes by 60 and the seconds by 3600 and add them to the degrees. For example 28° 36′ 50″ is 28 + 36/60 + 50/3600, which is about 28.6139. Enter negative numbers only for places south of the equator or west of the prime meridian, which does not apply to India."}]],null,null]}]
31:["$","div","Common mistakes",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"Common mistakes"}],[["$","p","The most common mistake is swapping latitude and",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"The most common mistake is swapping latitude and longitude. Latitude comes first and, for India, is the smaller number (between about 8 and 37); longitude comes second and is larger (between about 68 and 97). If the address shows an ocean or a different country, check the order. Other mistakes include using a comma instead of a decimal point, adding the degree symbol or letters like N and E to the boxes, and cutting digits so much that the point shifts by several hundred metres."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Latitude first, longitude second",{"children":"Latitude first, longitude second"}],["$","li","Use a decimal point and plain numbers only",{"children":"Use a decimal point and plain numbers only"}],["$","li","Keep at least four decimal places for street-level accuracy",{"children":"Keep at least four decimal places for street-level accuracy"}]]}],null]}]
